--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SCOPE

The MIT licence above covers the work original to this repository -- that is,
Copal Linux itself: copal-prep.sh, fetch-minivmac.sh, the scripts under
minivmac/, everything those generate (copal-init.sh and the helpers it installs
as copal, copal-menu, copal-center, copal-install, copal-guide and
copal-splash, plus the application catalogue and the guides), README.md and
lab-report.md.

"Copal Linux" is a name for this installer and its generated system.

RELATIONSHIP TO ALPINE LINUX -- Copal is an AGGREGATION of Alpine Linux, not a
derivative work of it. The distinction is the whole reason this section exists:

  * Copal contains no Alpine source code. Every script here is original work,
    and the licence above is a grant over that work alone.
  * copal-prep.sh DOWNLOADS stock Alpine from Alpine's own mirrors, verifies its
    published SHA256, and copies it onto a card unmodified. copal-init.sh then
    calls Alpine's own tools -- setup-alpine, setup-disk, apk, lbu -- rather
    than reimplementing them.
  * What ends up on the card is therefore an aggregate: Alpine, under Alpine's
    licences, plus Copal's scripts, under the MIT licence above. Each part keeps
    its own terms. Putting two works on one filesystem does not merge their
    licences, and nothing here attempts to.

Copal is NOT a fork of Alpine Linux and is not affiliated with or endorsed by
the Alpine Linux project.

ALPINE IS NOT MIT-LICENSED, and this must not be misread as claiming otherwise.
Alpine Linux is a distribution aggregating thousands of packages under many
licences. Among the pieces Copal relies on directly:

  Linux kernel        GPL-2.0-only (with the syscall exception)
  BusyBox             GPL-2.0-only
  apk-tools           GPL-2.0-only
  alpine-conf         MIT          (setup-alpine, setup-disk, setup-xorg-base)
  musl libc           MIT
  OpenRC              BSD-2-Clause

The MIT licence above CANNOT and does not relicense any of that. In particular,
no GPL-licensed component becomes MIT by being downloaded, installed or invoked
by an MIT-licensed script -- and the applications Copal's catalogue installs
(GIMP, Wireshark, GNU Radio, GHC and some three hundred others) each remain
under their own terms, which the catalogue never alters.

If you redistribute a card or image written by Copal, you are redistributing
those components, and their licences -- including the GPL's source-offer
obligations -- apply to you for those parts.

It does NOT and cannot cover the third-party material stored alongside them.
Each of these remains under its own terms, and nothing here relicenses any of
it:

  work/alpine-rpi-*            Alpine Linux, and the packages inside it, under
  work/alpine-netboot-*        their respective licences (mostly GPL, MIT, BSD).
  work/alpine-virt-*.iso       See https://alpinelinux.org/
                               The virt ISO is downloaded on the x86 path for one
                               file: efi/boot/bootx64.efi, Alpine's build of GRUB
                               (GPL-3.0-or-later), copied to the card unmodified.

  minivmac/minivmac-*.src.tgz  Mini vMac, (c) Paul C. Pratt and contributors,
  minivmac/copyroms-*.zip      GPL-2.0. See https://www.gryphel.com/c/minivmac/
  minivmac/blanks-*.zip

  minivmac/System_7.0.1.smi.bin  Apple Macintosh system software.
  minivmac/macOS755.dsk*         Copyright Apple Inc. Not redistributable.

  minivmac/vMac.ROM            Macintosh Plus ROM. Copyright Apple Inc.
                               Never distributed by Apple, and not
                               redistributable. Present here only as a dump of
                               hardware owned by the repository's owner.

Publishing this repository — pushing it to a public remote, for instance —
would distribute the Apple material above, which the MIT licence does not
permit and cannot authorise. If this repository is ever to be made public, the
Apple files must be removed from the working tree AND from git history first,
since history retains every committed blob.
